derdog at +237; the total closed at 54.5 and they combined for 42, under by 12.5."],"review":[{"title":"The algo's call","body":"Logged before the start, last snapshot Nov 23, 8:14 PM ET. It had Bengals 74% and Commanders 26%, projecting Bengals 29.1 – Commanders 20.8 (49.9 total, Bengals by 8.3).\n\nFinal: Bengals 20 – Commanders 22. Wrong winner: it had Bengals at 74%, and Commanders (26%) won."},{"title":"How the ratings held up","body":"Bengals came in with a 17% above average attack and a league-average defense (7-2, 30.9 scored and 21.4 allowed a game over 9 games), worth about 51 and 53 games of evidence. Projected to score 29.1, they scored 20 (−9.1 points, 31% under); projected to allow 20.8, they allowed 22 (+1.2 points, 6% over).\n\nCommanders came in with a 3% below average attack and a 4% leakier than average defense (3-5-1, 21.8 scored and 24.8 allowed a game over 9 games), worth about 50 and 54 games of evidence. Projected to score 20.8, they scored 22 (+1.2 points, 6% over); projected to allow 29.1, they allowed 20 (−9.1 points, 31% under).\n\nThe bigger miss was Bengals' scoring (-9.1 points against projection)."},{"title":"Where the result sat in the simulations","body":"Total: 42 against 49.9 projected (-7.9), about the 27th percentile of the simulated totals (a typical game swings ±13.2).\n\nMargin: Commanders by 2 against Bengals by 8.3 projected, about the 79th percentile of the simulated margins (typical swing ±12.8).\n\nAn ordinary result: inside the range the simulations expected most of the time."},{"title":"Situational factors, checked","body":"Weather (57°F · ? mph wind): Commanders ×0.94, Bengals ×0.94. Market (Line movement signal): Commanders ×1.00, Bengals ×1.02. It favored Bengals, who did not beat their projection by more than the other side did."},{"title":"Against the market","body":"WSH ML (+245) at +245: the algo gave it 28% vs 28% fair (-0.2 pts) — won (+2.5u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 29%). CIN ML (-301) at -301: the algo gave it 72% vs 72% fair (+0.2 pts) — lost (-1u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 71%). WSH +6 (+100) at +100: the algo gave it 48% vs 48% fair (-0.3 pts) — won (+1u); same number as the close. CIN -6 (-120) at -120: the algo gave it 52% vs 52% fair (+0.3 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. OVER 54.5 (-111) at -111: the algo gave it 49% vs 50% fair (-1.4 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. UNDER 54.5 (-108) at -108: the algo gave it 51% vs 50% fair (+1.4 pts) — won (+0.9u); same number as the close.\n\nThe line barely moved between the algo's snapshot and the close.\n\nNo bet: nothing cleared the algo's bar before the game."},{"title":"Where the public and the money were","body":"Splits (Action Network): spread: 72% of bets on Bengals, 75% of the money — Commanders covered; total: 57% of bets on the over, 56% of the money — it went under; moneyline: 92% of bets on Bengals, 84% of the money.\n\nThe sharp side by the algo's read was Bengals, who lost and didn't cover."},{"title":"What the algo learns","body":"This game's own lesson: scoring came in at ×0.832 of the raw projection, and the home side beat its projected margin by +9.3 points. It counts toward NFL scoring level, home edge and both teams' attack and defense corrections.\n\nAcross 55 graded NFL games the algo now scales scoring ×0.986 and gives home teams -0.9 points. Team corrections so far: Bengals attack ×1.036, defense ×0.969 (4 games); Commanders attack ×0.979, defense ×0.963 (3 games)."},{"title":"Bottom line","body":"Wrong side, total within its normal range, margin within its normal range, no bet."}],"archived":"2026-11-24T04:20:06.637Z"}}}